+# Continuation power flow — pypowsybl port (Phase-1 prototype)
+
+Experimental, OpenLoadFlow-specific analysis that traces the P–V "nose" curve to the voltage-collapse point.
+This branch stands up the **shape** of the port end-to-end. The Java C-API layer and the Python module are
+written in full; the C++/pybind glue is provided below as ready-to-paste snippets (it can only be compiled as
+part of the GraalVM `native-image` + CMake build, so it is not applied to the tracked build files yet).
+
+## What's implemented on this branch
+
+| Layer | File | Status |
+|---|---|---|
+| Java C entry points | `java/pypowsybl/src/main/java/com/powsybl/python/continuation/ContinuationCFunctions.java` | complete |
+| Java result → dataframes | `.../continuation/ContinuationDataframes.java` | complete |
+| Python package | `pypowsybl/continuation/` (`__init__`, `impl/parameters.py`, `impl/continuation.py`, `impl/continuation_result.py`) | complete |
+| Module registration | `pypowsybl/__init__.py` | complete |
+| C++ wrapper + pybind | snippets below | to apply during build |
+| C ABI header | auto-generated by `native-image` from the `@CEntryPoint`s | — |
+
+The design mirrors **security analysis**: `run_continuation_power_flow(...)` returns a result *handle*, and the
+curve / breakpoints / summary are read back as pandas DataFrames via the generic series-array machinery. It is
+the first pypowsybl C-API to call an OpenLoadFlow class directly (`ContinuationAnalysis`) instead of a
+powsybl-core provider SPI — worth confirming with a maintainer.
+
+## Blocker: OpenLoadFlow version
+
+`com.powsybl.openloadflow.ac.continuation.*` is only in open-loadflow **2.3.0-SNAPSHOT** (unreleased). pypowsybl
+pins open-loadflow transitively through `powsybl-dependencies 2026.0.0`. Until the continuation work is released,
+build against a local snapshot:
+
+```bash
+# 1. install the open-loadflow snapshot that contains the continuation package
+cd /path/to/powsybl-open-loadflow      # branch: claude/loadflow-continuation-voltage-collapse-5gzt52
+./mvnw -DskipTests install              # publishes 2.3.0-SNAPSHOT to ~/.m2
+
+# 2. pin that version in pypowsybl's java module (override the BOM)
+#    java/pypowsybl/pom.xml, in the <dependency> for powsybl-open-loadflow:
+#      <artifactId>powsybl-open-loadflow</artifactId>
+#      <version>2.3.0-SNAPSHOT</version>   <!-- add this line -->
+```
+
+## C++ glue to apply
+
+### `cpp/powsybl-cpp/powsybl-cpp.h` — declarations (near the other loadflow/security decls)
+
+```cpp
+JavaHandle runContinuationPowerFlow(const JavaHandle& network, int engine, double initialStepSize,
+                                    double minStepSize, int maxSteps, bool enforceReactiveLimits,
+                                    bool scaleReactivePowerWithActivePower,
+                                    const std::string& loadIds, const std::string& generatorIds);
+SeriesArray* getContinuationCurve(const JavaHandle& result);
+SeriesArray* getContinuationBreakpoints(const JavaHandle& result);
+SeriesArray* getContinuationSummary(const JavaHandle& result);
+void freeContinuationResult(const JavaHandle& result);
+```
+
+### `cpp/powsybl-cpp/powsybl-cpp.cpp` — implementations
+
+```cpp
+JavaHandle runContinuationPowerFlow(const JavaHandle& network, int engine, double initialStepSize,
+                                    double minStepSize, int maxSteps, bool enforceReactiveLimits,
+                                    bool scaleReactivePowerWithActivePower,
+                                    const std::string& loadIds, const std::string& generatorIds) {
+    return PowsyblCaller::get()->callJava<JavaHandle>(::runContinuationPowerFlow, network, engine,
+        initialStepSize, minStepSize, maxSteps, enforceReactiveLimits, scaleReactivePowerWithActivePower,
+        (char*) loadIds.data(), (char*) generatorIds.data());
+}
+SeriesArray* getContinuationCurve(const JavaHandle& result) {
+    return new SeriesArray(PowsyblCaller::get()->callJava<array*>(::getContinuationCurve, result));
+}
+SeriesArray* getContinuationBreakpoints(const JavaHandle& result) {
+    return new SeriesArray(PowsyblCaller::get()->callJava<array*>(::getContinuationBreakpoints, result));
+}
+SeriesArray* getContinuationSummary(const JavaHandle& result) {
+    return new SeriesArray(PowsyblCaller::get()->callJava<array*>(::getContinuationSummary, result));
+}
+void freeContinuationResult(const JavaHandle& result) {
+    PowsyblCaller::get()->callJava<>(::freeContinuationResult, result);
+}
+```
+
+### `cpp/pypowsybl-cpp/bindings.cpp` — pybind11 module defs (in `PYBIND11_MODULE`)
+
+```cpp
+m.def("run_continuation_power_flow", &pypowsybl::runContinuationPowerFlow,
+      "Run a continuation power flow and return a result handle",
+      py::arg("network"), py::arg("engine"), py::arg("initial_step_size"), py::arg("min_step_size"),
+      py::arg("max_steps"), py::arg("enforce_reactive_limits"), py::arg("scale_reactive_power_with_active_power"),
+      py::arg("load_ids"), py::arg("generator_ids"));
+m.def("get_continuation_curve", &pypowsybl::getContinuationCurve, "P-V curve dataframe", py::arg("result"));
+m.def("get_continuation_breakpoints", &pypowsybl::getContinuationBreakpoints, "Reactive-limit breakpoints", py::arg("result"));
+m.def("get_continuation_summary", &pypowsybl::getContinuationSummary, "Collapse summary dataframe", py::arg("result"));
+m.def("free_continuation_result", &pypowsybl::freeContinuationResult, "Free a continuation result handle", py::arg("result"));
+```
+
+The `::runContinuationPowerFlow` (etc.) C symbols are emitted automatically into the generated
+`pypowsybl-java.h` when `native-image` processes the new `@CEntryPoint`s — no hand-editing of a C header.
+
+## Build
+
+```bash
+pip install -r requirements.txt
+python setup.py develop        # drives CMake: mvn package → native-image → powsybl-cpp → _pypowsybl
+```
+
+## Smoke test (once built)
+
+```python
+import pypowsybl.network as pn
+import pypowsybl.continuation as continuation
+from pypowsybl.continuation import ContinuationParameters, ContinuationEngine
+
+network = pn.create_eurostag_tutorial_example1_network()
+result = continuation.run(network, ContinuationParameters(engine=ContinuationEngine.PREDICTOR_CORRECTOR))
+
+print(result.status)             # NOSE_POINT_REACHED
+print(result.max_load_factor)    # ~0.86 (loadability margin)
+print(result.critical_bus_id)    # the collapse-driving bus
+result.pv_curve(result.critical_bus_id)  # plottable DataFrame: load_factor, voltage, dv_dlambda, stable
+```
+
+A matching pytest lives at `tests/test_continuation.py`.
+
+## Follow-ups before this is production
+
+- Release the continuation code in open-loadflow so the BOM resolves it (removes the version override).
+- Decide whether to keep the direct-OLF-class dependency or introduce a thin SPI in core/OLF.
+- Promote continuation parameters from primitive C args to a proper `@CStruct` (mirrors loadflow) if the knob
+  set grows; add JSON round-trip and provider-specific parameter discovery.
+- Docs page under `docs/reference/` and an example notebook.
